                    briefing_text_r1:       `Two demand worlds, one supply chain. Your <strong>basics</strong> — classic tents and daypacks, ~60% of volume — are stable, predictable and price-sensitive: a textbook <em>lean</em> line. Your <strong>performance / seasonal</strong> range is volatile, short-lived and margin-rich: a textbook <em>agile</em> line. VOEC has run <strong>one</strong> long, cheap lean chain for both — and that single design is why you are short the viral tent (fill 61%) and long US$22M of slow basics at once. Classify the portfolio by demand type, then place VOEC on Goldsby's three resilience dimensions: <strong>preparedness, alertness, agility</strong>. You found out about the port strike from a retailer's complaint — three weeks late.`,
