                    insight_resilient:      `Resilient configuration: you solved the mismatch as one design — lean basics, agile performance, a decoupling point, selective buffers and alertness as standing capability. Fill rate is restored, the agility index is high, the line held, and the design helps against the next shock you cannot name yet.`,
                    insight_breach:         `Covenant breached: inventory ran over the US$110M line. Whatever fill rate you recovered, you financed it with headroom you did not have — the blanket-buffer reflex is exactly what the bank warned about. Selective buffering matched to variability would have bought the same service for far less cash.`,
                    insight_singleshock:    `Single-shock patch: your plan solves this port strike and this viral tent, but little of it is standing capability. The next disruption — a supplier fire, a tariff, a demand collapse — will catch you rebuilding from scratch. Resilience is durable optionality, not reactive firefighting.`,
                    insight_short:          `You did not fully reconcile the configuration. The lean/agile split, the buffers and the alertness investment still pull in slightly different directions — enough that the next shock finds the seam.`,
                    insight_fill_low:       `Fill rate stayed below target: either the lean chain could not catch the viral window, or buffer and expedite were too thin where demand was variable. The full-margin demand you missed is the most expensive line item of all.`,
                    insight_fill_target:    `Fill rate is back at target: you served the hot SKU through the agile chain and a margin-tested expedite without starving it — the right service on the right products.`,
                    insight_tlc_high:       `Total logistics cost ran high: indiscriminate air freight, all-agile sourcing on basics, or trapped slow inventory all added cost the unit price never showed. The cheapest source can be the most expensive supply chain.`,
                    insight_tlc_saved:      `Total logistics cost actually fell versus the status quo — the leagile split and a disciplined margin test bought service while taking cost out, exactly the total-cost-of-ownership win the design promised.`,
                    insight_blind:          `You bought responsiveness but never built alertness — speed you cannot aim. Agility and alertness are distinct dimensions; without visibility you will react late to the next shock no matter how fast your chain can move.`,
                    insight_leagile:        `Your decoupling point plus alertness is the durable core: lean upstream where demand is forecastable, agile downstream where it is not, with the visibility to see the next shock early. That configuration outlasts this quarter.`,

                    hint_breach:            `You have breached or are at the working-capital line. Inventory above US$110M is the covenant trigger — pull the buffer back and target it on the variable SKUs only.`,
